    "paragraph": "To analyze speeding behavior at the OpenStreetMap way ID level, one study developed a scalable data pipeline that processes connected vehicle trajectory data and fills in missing speed limits. Another paper introduced a domain adaptation framework to estimate intersection turning movement counts by combining traffic-controller-event-based data, road infrastructure data, and point-of-interest data. Finally, researchers developed the Trajectory Refinement for Emission Modeling framework, which uses mixed-integer quadratic programming to post-process microsimulated vehicle trajectories and eliminate nonphysical acceleration and jerk fluctuations.",
